.\" Manpage for yore.
.TH YORE 1 "2026-06-15" "yore" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
yore \- project-aware, frecency-ranked, team-shareable shell command memory
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B yore
[\fIflags\fR]
.br
.B yore here
[\fIflags\fR]
.br
.B yore
\fIsubcommand\fR [\fIargs\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B yore
turns your shell history into useful memory. It ranks the commands you reuse by
.IR frecency
(frequency and recency combined), scopes them to the current project, knows
which ones exited successfully, and lets you save commands as named,
parameterized
.IR recipes
that can be committed and shared with a team.
.PP
Install the recording hook with
.B yore init
to capture each command's directory, exit status and duration. Until then,
.B yore
reads your existing shell history. yore is local-only: no daemon, no database,
no network. Commands that look like they contain secrets are never recorded.
.SH FLAGS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-top " " \fIN\fR
Limit output to the top \fIN\fR commands (0 = all).
.TP
.B \-\-here
Scope recall to the current project (same as
.BR "yore here" ).
.TP
.B \-\-ok
Only commands that have exited successfully.
.TP
.BR \-\-sort " " \fIMODE\fR
Ordering: \fBfrecency\fR (default), \fBrecent\fR, \fBfrequent\fR or \fBraw\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-half\-life " " \fIDUR\fR
Frecency decay half-life, e.g. \fB720h\fR (default, 30 days).
.TP
.BR \-\-min\-count " " \fIN\fR
Only commands used at least \fIN\fR times.
.TP
.B \-\-count
Prefix each line with its usage count (TAB-separated).
.TP
.B \-\-redact
Drop commands that look like they contain secrets.
.TP
.BR \-\-file " " \fIPATH\fR
Read a specific history file instead of recorded memory (repeatable; use
.B \-
for standard input).
.TP
.BR \-0 ", " \-\-null
Separate entries with NUL instead of newline.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B here
Recall commands used in the current project.
.TP
.B pick
Fuzzy-pick a command or recipe and print it (bound to Ctrl-G by
.BR "yore init" ).
.TP
.BI "save " "name " "\-\- " command
Save a command as a reusable recipe. Use \fB{placeholders}\fR for variable
parts. Flags: \fB\-\-desc\fR, \fB\-\-last\fR (use the most recent command),
\fB\-\-project\fR (write to ./.yorefile).
.TP
.BI "run " name
Run a saved recipe, prompting for parameters.
Flags: \fB\-\-print\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR.
.TP
.B recipes
List saved recipes.
.TP
.BI "init " shell
Print shell integration for bash, zsh or fish (eval/source it).
.TP
.B import
Seed memory from existing shell history files.
.TP
.BI "completion " shell
Output a bash, zsh or fish completion script.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.local/share/yore/history.jsonl
Recorded command events (private).
.TP
.B ~/.config/yore/recipes
Personal recipes.
.TP
.B ./.yorefile
Per-project recipes (commit to share with your team).
.SH RANKING
Each unique command is scored as
.IR count " " \(mu " 2^(\-" age " / " half-life ),
so a command used many times long ago can be outranked by one used a few times
recently. History without timestamps falls back to pure frequency.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B yore here --ok
Commands that worked, in the current project.
.TP
.B yore save --project deploy -- ./deploy.sh --env '{env}'
Save a team recipe with an {env} parameter.
.TP
.B yore run deploy
Run it, prompting for {env}.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success (including a closed downstream pipe and a cancelled picker).
.TP
.B 1
A runtime error.
.TP
.B 2
A usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fzf (1),
.BR history (1)
.SH HOMEPAGE
https://github.com/indihood/yore
